<title>BELGIUM: EU clears TAP Air Portugal 40 billion escudos aid.</title>
<headline>EU clears TAP Air Portugal 40 billion escudos aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday cleared the final 40 billion-escudo tranche of government aid to TAP Air Portugal, a Commission official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The aid payment, cleared without discussion at the weekly meeting of European Commissioners, is part of a package worth 180 billion escudos to the Portuguese state airline, which the Commission originally cleared in July 1994.</p>
<p>A senior Commission official said last Friday that the airline's performance was on course as foreseen in the original authorisation, opening the way for Wednesday's clearance.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
